{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[{"left":"900","quote":"\\[\n360 + 180 + 180 + 180 = 800\n\\]","right":"800","span":[1847,1880]}],"prefix":"To solve the problem, we need to find the values of \\(x\\) such that \\(\\sin x^\\circ = \\sin x\\) radians. We start by converting \\(x\\) degrees to radians, knowing that \\(x^\\circ = \\frac{\\pi x}{180}\\) radians. Thus, we need to solve the equation:\n\n\\[\n\\sin \\left( \\frac{\\pi x}{180} \\right) = \\sin x\n\\]\n\nThe sine function is periodic and has the property that \\(\\sin \\theta = \\sin (\\pi - \\theta)\\). Therefore, we have two cases to consider:\n\n1. \\(\\frac{\\pi x}{180} = x + 2k\\pi\\) for some integer \\(k\\)\n2. \\(\\frac{\\pi x}{180} = \\pi - x + 2k\\pi\\) for some integer \\(k\\)\n\n**Case 1: \\(\\frac{\\pi x}{180} = x + 2k\\pi\\)**\nRearranging terms, we get:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\pi x}{180} - x = 2k\\pi \\implies \\left( \\frac{\\pi}{180} - 1 \\right)x = 2k\\pi \\implies x \\left( \\frac{\\pi - 180}{180} \\right) = 2k\\pi \\implies x = \\frac{360k\\pi}{180 - \\pi}\n\\]\nWe are looking for the least positive real values of \\(x\\), so we set \\(k = 1\\):\n\\[\nx = \\frac{360\\pi}{180 - \\pi}\n\\]\n\n**Case 2: \\(\\frac{\\pi x}{180} = \\pi - x + 2k\\pi\\)**\nRearranging terms, we get:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\pi x}{180} + x = \\pi + 2k\\pi \\implies x \\left( \\frac{\\pi}{180} + 1 \\right) = \\pi (1 + 2k) \\implies x = \\frac{180 \\pi (1 + 2k)}{\\pi + 180}\n\\]\nFor the least positive real value, we set \\(k = 0\\):\n\\[\nx = \\frac{180 \\pi}{\\pi + 180}\n\\]\n\nWe are given that the two least positive real values of \\(x\\) are \\(\\frac{m\\pi}{n-\\pi}\\) and \\(\\frac{p\\pi}{q+\\pi}\\). Comparing with our solutions, we have:\n\\[\n\\frac{360\\pi}{180 - \\pi} = \\frac{m\\pi}{n - \\pi} \\implies \\frac{360}{180 - \\pi} = \\frac{m}{n - \\pi} \\implies m = 360, \\quad n - \\pi = 180 - \\pi \\implies n = 180\n\\]\n\\[\n\\frac{180 \\pi}{\\pi + 180} = \\frac{p\\pi}{q + \\pi} \\implies \\frac{180}{\\pi + 180} = \\frac{p}{q + \\pi} \\implies p = 180, \\quad q + \\pi = \\pi + 180 \\implies q = 180\n\\]\n\nThus, we have \\(m = 360\\), \\(n = 180\\), \\(p = 180\\), and \\(q = 180\\). The sum \\(m + n + p + q\\) is:\n\\[\n360 + 180 + 180 + 180 = 800\n\\]\n\n","prefix_end":1882,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":true,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,279,3491,11,582,1184,311,1477,279,2750,315,17767,87,57758,1741,429,1124,11520,15940,856,24884,43298,284,1124,15940,856,57758,50784,13,1205,1191,553,33437,17767,87,57758,12348,311,50784,11,14063,429,17767,87,24884,43298,284,1124,37018,35702,2493,856,15170,16,23,15,11035,8,50784,13,14301,11,582,1184,311,11625,279,23606,1447,59,9640,59,15940,1124,2359,7,1124,37018,35702,2493,856,15170,16,23,15,92,1124,1291,8,284,1124,15940,856,198,59,2533,785,57668,729,374,38345,323,702,279,3343,429,1124,11520,15940,1124,15976,284,1124,15940,19788,2493,481,1124,15976,10699,568,15277,11,582,614,1378,5048,311,2908,1447,16,13,1124,11520,37018,35702,2493,856,15170,16,23,15,92,284,856,488,220,17,74,59,2493,57758,369,1045,7546,17767,74,59,340,17,13,1124,11520,37018,35702,2493,856,15170,16,23,15,92,284,1124,2493,481,856,488,220,17,74,59,2493,57758,369,1045,7546,17767,74,59,692,334,4207,220,16,25,1124,11520,37018,35702,2493,856,15170,16,23,15,92,284,856,488,220,17,74,59,2493,57758,1019,49,682,81,8595,3793,11,582,633,510,59,9640,59,37018,35702,2493,856,15170,16,23,15,92,481,856,284,220,17,74,59,2493,1124,6383,550,1124,2359,7,1124,37018,35702,2493,15170,16,23,15,92,481,220,16,1124,1291,50724,284,220,17,74,59,2493,1124,6383,550,856,1124,2359,7,1124,37018,35702,2493,481,220,16,23,15,15170,16,23,15,92,1124,1291,8,284,220,17,74,59,2493,1124,6383,550,856,284,1124,37018,90,18,21,15,74,59,2493,15170,16,23,15,481,1124,2493,532,59,921,1654,525,3330,369,279,3245,6785,1931,2750,315,17767,87,59,701,773,582,738,17767,74,284,220,16,59,982,59,9640,87,284,1124,37018,90,18,21,15,59,2493,15170,16,23,15,481,112